299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 149 0 R
/T (1.3 Why this finding may not have been visible before)
/E (1.3 Why this finding may not have been visible before)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Two working hypotheses. First, a meaningful share of the Indian outbound research in public circulation originates with booking platforms \(MakeMyTrip, Yatra, EaseMyTrip\) whose primary data captures the moment of transaction, at which point price and convenience are necessarily dominant. Transaction-anchored research methodologically understates the upstream inspiration moment that precedes the transaction by a median of 47 recalled days, as documented in Section 7 of this report.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Second, tourism boards that have conducted India studies have typically used methodologies designed for established outbound markets \(United States, United Kingdom, Germany\), where consideration sets are smaller, decision windows are shorter, and the role of creator content in the funnel is less pronounced. The Indian outbound traveller in 2026 is structurally different: she is younger, she is more likely to be a first-time outbound traveller, she is heavily creator-content-immersed, and she shops a consideration set of seven to twelve destinations against any single trip.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Our methodology captured both the upstream inspiration moment and the downstream transaction moment, in the same panel, with the same respondents, and traced the path between them. That linkage is the principal methodological contribution of this report.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 149 0 R
/T (1.4 The two non-obvious sub-findings)
/E (1.4 The two non-obvious sub-findings)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Sub-finding A: Inspiration is durable. When asked to recall the inspiration that triggered their most recent international trip, 78% of respondents could name a specific creator, film, or moment more than six months after the inspiration event. Paid campaigns, by contrast, had a 14% unaided recall rate after the same six-month window. Inspiration is not just a stronger trigger; it is a more durable one.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Sub-finding B: Inspiration is increasingly multi-modal. 41% of respondents reported that their last destination decision involved at least two distinct inspiration sources, for example an Instagram Reel followed by an OTT show set in the same destination, or a friend's post followed by a creator's long-form YouTube travel documentary. The multi-modal inspiration journey, not the single-touch trigger, is now the dominant path to Indian outbound booking. Within inspiration specifically, 66% of attributed consideration concentrates in three channels  Instagram, YouTube, and ShareChat  as documented in Section 4. \(Note the two different denominators: 67% and 6% are shares of all respondents; the 66% is a share of inspiration-attributed consideration.\))
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E ("I saw a Hong Kong reel from a creator I follow, then my cousin posted from there a month later, then I saw it again on a JioHotstar show. By the third time, I knew I was going.")
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
