<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Inspiration is self-reported. Respondents may unconsciously assign credit to channels they find more flattering to recall \(creator content\) versus more banal \(repeated paid-ad exposure\). We mitigated through structured probes but cannot fully eliminate the bias. Indian outbound demographics are evolving rapidly. Findings represent a Q1 2026 snapshot. A durability re-contact wave \(scheduled Q4 2026\) will assess how much not-yet-booked intent converts.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (This report measures consideration and booking intent, not actual conversion or arrivals. Arrivals data must come from destination NTOs and immigration sources, which we triangulate against in destination-specific consulting work but not in this report. Sample weighting is conservative. Where panel demographics deviated from published Indian outbound demographics, we down-weighted oversamples rather than up-weighting undersamples, preserving statistical robustness at the cost of some precision in undersampled cells.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
