583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (A note on cohort construction: the six cohorts are editorial-analytical personas, not strict statistical clusters. They were derived by combining \(a\) k-means clustering on the panel's channel-attribution and time-to-booking variables, which surfaced five natural clusters, with \(b\) marketing-segmentation judgment that separated destination-wedding behaviour from other premium-couple behaviour, given its distinct decision pattern, yielding six profiled cohorts. Each label mixes demographic, behavioural, and destination-preference attributes intentionally: the labels are designed to be usable by tourism-board marketers rather than statistically pure. Readers seeking the underlying unweighted statistical clusters may request the supplementary appendix at research@melangedigital.co.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
