>>
endobj
844 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (At first contact, a substantial share of inspired-and-considered destinations sat in an unresolved state: the respondent had moved a destination into the consideration set but had not yet booked it. Because the median inspiration-to-booking journey runs 47 days with a long right-hand tail, and a meaningful minority of journeys extend well beyond three months, a single short-window measurement understates how much of this intent eventually converts. To quantify that conversion directly, a durability re-contact of consented respondents \(n = 1,180\) is scheduled for a Q4 2026 wave, measuring how much not-yet-booked intent resolves into confirmed bookings at a 9-to-14-month horizon measured from the original inspiration event \(which for most respondents predates fielding\). The forward implication for tourism boards is already directionally clear from the booking-time distribution: attribution should be measured on a horizon of up to 18 months, not solely the 90-day window common in paid-media measurement, or a large share of inspiration-driven conversions will fall outside the measurement frame entirely.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
