865 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Failure 01: Treating India as one market)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
866 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (62% of NTO India campaigns in the panel sample were variants of the same creative across the country. Tier-segmentation, language-segmentation, and cohort-segmentation are routinely absent. India behaves as several distinct markets: this report profiles six traveller cohorts \(five statistically derived, one added by segmentation judgment\), as set out in Section 5, and a meaningful destination strategy treats them as such.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
867 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 168 0 R
/T (Failure 02: Single-narrative dependence)
/E (Failure 02: Single-narrative dependence)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
868 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Destinations known to Indian audiences for one thing \(the Pyramids, the Eiffel Tower, the Vegas Strip\) over-rely on the headline asset and underdevelop secondary narratives. Single-narrative destinations score 31% lower on "would return within 3 years" than multi-narrative destinations with comparable absolute appeal.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
869 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 168 0 R
/T (Failure 03: Buying paid display before earning creator velocity)
/E (Failure 03: Buying paid display before earning creator velocity)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
870 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (A directional recommendation rather than a quantified rule: NTO India spend in 2025 concentrated heavily in paid-display formats \(programmatic OOH, paid social, sponsored content\). Our sample finding, that paid-display recall and stated message attribution were approximately 37% lower among respondents reporting concurrent creator exposure for the same destination, is a correlation in self-reported recall, not a controlled experimental result. The directional implication is that paid display sequenced after creator inspiration is plausibly more effective than concurrent or pre-creator deployment. Most NTOs we observe do the reverse. A/B field testing in live campaigns would validate the magnitude.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
871 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 168 0 R
/T (Failure 04: Mistaking trade engagement for consumer demand)
/E (Failure 04: Mistaking trade engagement for consumer demand)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
872 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Trade shows, agent FAMs, and B2B engagement are necessary but not sufficient. The panel data shows tour-operator influence is meaningful only at the bottom of the funnel \(Day 28 onward\): operators close trips; they do not start them. NTOs that lead with trade and follow with consumer are routinely overtaken by NTOs that lead with creator-led consumer engagement and pull trade along.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [8]
>>
