/E (Consider reallocating a meaningful portion \(we hypothesise 35% to 55%\) of current paid India destination marketing spend to creator-led activation over the next 12 months. The hypothesis is grounded in the sample-observed gap between the 6% of respondents who cited a destination marketing campaign as a trigger and the 67% who cited inspiration, of which 66% of attributed consideration concentrates in Instagram, YouTube, and ShareChat. The optimal reallocation will vary by destination starting position, existing creator inventory, and budget elasticity; ROI modelling for the specific NTO is recommended before implementing a fixed-percentage shift.)
/Pg 36 0 R
